	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: Deep-learning algorithms were used to “automatically segment and quantify five different body tissues and cardiopulmonary features” from CT, while the actual survival prediction models were Cox proportional-hazards models integrating CT, demographic, and clinical variables. Since ML/CNN primarily enabled feature extraction and the main survival model was Cox regression, Primary ML Component is best classified as Other. Validation used 5-fold cross-validation for time-point survival classification. Feature selection in the multivariate CPH models used backward-stepwise regression. I did not see explicit hyperparameter tuning for the CNN or Cox models in the retrieved text.  ￼

